hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9901","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Al-Aziz, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that he wanted to bid farewell to a man, so he said: Come, I will bid you farewell, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did. He bid us farewell: “I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your deeds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9902","Al-Hasan bin Ismail told me, Abdah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar, on the authority of Yahya bin Ismail, Qaza’ah told us, On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, bade farewell to a man and said: “I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your deeds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9903","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ismail bin Jarir, on the authority of Qaza’ah, He said: Ibn Umar sent me to do something, so he took my hand and said: Come, I bid you farewell as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bid me farewell, and he sent me to He was in need, so he said: “I entrust to God your religion, your trust, and the end of your work.”"
"9904","Ahmad bin Harb told us, Abu Damra told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Yahya bin Ismail Ibn Jarir, on the authority of Qazah, he said: I was with Abdullah Ibn Omar and I wanted to leave, so he said: As you are, until I bid you farewell as the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, bid farewell to me. May God bless him and grant him peace, so he took my hand and shook my hand, then said: “I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the seals of your deeds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9905","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, I am Issa, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz, Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad told me, on the authority of Qaza’ah, he said: I came to Ibn Umar to bid him farewell, and he said: I bid you farewell as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bid me farewell. So he took my hand and moved it, and said: “I entrust to God your religion, your trust, and the end of your work.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9906","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya, Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz told me, on the authority of Qaza’ah, that Ibn Omar told him When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bid farewell to him, he said: “I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your deeds.”"
"9907","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Nahshal bin Mujma’ al-Dhabi, on the authority of Qaza’ah, he said: I was with Ibn Umar. When I left, he turned to me and said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Luqman the Wise said: If God entrusts something, He preserves it. And I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your deeds, and I extend my peace upon you.”"
"9908","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Sulayman informed us, Abdah informed us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Nahshal Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Qaza’ah, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Luqman the Wise used to say: When God entrusts something, He preserves it.”"
"9909","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, Suwayd told us, Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, Nahshal bin Mujma’ told me, and he was satisfactory, about Qaza’ah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed us: “Luqman the Wise used to say: When God entrusts something \save it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9910","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, Ishaq bin al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nahshal, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, he said: Qaza’ah Ibn Umar and I joined the funeral procession, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us: “Luqman the Wise said: Indeed, when God is entrusted He preserved something, and I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your deeds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9911","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, Suwayd told us, Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Qaza’ah, and Abu Ghalib, They said: We took Ibn Umar on our way, and when we wanted to separate from him, he said: “I do not have anything to give you, but I entrust your religion and your trusts to God.” And the end of your deeds, and I extend my greetings to you both.” Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, Ubayd Allah told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, he said: I was with Ibn Omar and Qaza’a, and when we left him, he walked with us, then said: I do not have anything to give you, but I entrust God, and he continued the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9912","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Hanzalah, I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad say: A man wanted to go on a journey. Then he came to greet Abdullah bin Omar, and Abdullah bin Omar said: Wait until I bid you farewell, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bid us farewell: “I entrust to God your religion, your trust, and the end of your work.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9913","Muhammad bin Ubaid told me, Sa`id bin Khuthaym told me, Hanzalah told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, he said: Whenever my father saw The man, as he wanted to travel, said: Come close to him so that I may bid you farewell, just as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bid us farewell. Then he said: “I bid farewell to God.” Your religion, your trustworthiness, and the end of your work.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9914","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, I heard Jarir saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Isn’t that khalasa enough for me?” I said: O Messenger of God, I am a man who is not steadfast on horses. So he struck my chest and said: “O God, make him steadfast.” And make him a guide, a guide.” So I went out with fifty of my people, and we went to it and burned it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9915","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Peace be upon him, while he was on his way, and a boy of his called Anjasha was leading the people. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Woe to you, Anjasha.” \Slowly"," I will drive you with bottles.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9916","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, came to Anjasha while he was driving his wives, and he said: “Take your drive, and do not break the bottles.”"
"9917","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, Abd al-Samad told us, Hammam told us, Qatada told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: It was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He had a sharp, beautiful voice, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Take it easy, O Anjasha, do not break the bottles.” Weakness of women (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9918","Amr bin Ali told us, Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Thabit, he said: I heard Anas, saying: While The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking and riding alone with the wives of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was saying: “Oh Angsha, take the bottles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9919","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Suleiman. And Muhammad bin Mansour told us, and the wording for it, he said: Sufyan told us, Sulayman al-Taymi told us, I heard Anas bin Malik, saying: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has a sharp man called Anjasha. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was driving with the mothers of the believers: Take your time, Angsha, drive you with bottles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9920","Muhammad bin Maadan told us, Zuhayr told us, Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of his mother, that she was with the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and a driver was driving with them, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Slowly, oh, the freshest of your drives in bottles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9921","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Al-Hasan bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Muzani, On the authority of Abu Sakhrah Jami` ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Masoud, he said: “He was with us The night the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept and missed the morning prayer, until the sun rose at two o’clock.”"
"9922","Ahmad bin Abi Ubayd Allah Al-Basri, who was called Al-Warraq, told us. Omar bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rawaha, that he was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his way, and he said to him: “O Ibn Rawaha, come down So he moved the stirrups. He said: O Messenger of God, I have left that one. Omar said: Listen and obey. He said: He threw himself down and said: Oh God, had it not been for you. We have not been guided, nor have we given alms, nor have we prayed. They have sent down tranquility upon us, and steadfastness of our feet when we meet them."
"9923","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, Mukhlid told us, Yunus told us, on the authority of his father, Al-Baraa bin Azib told me, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, moved the dirt from the ditch until the hair of his chest could see the dirt, and he was shaking the words of Abdullah bin Rawaha, O God. Were it not for You, we would not have been guided, nor would we have given alms, nor prayed. So send down upon us tranquility and firmness of footing if we meet us. Indeed, they have transgressed against us, even if they wanted. Our father’s temptation, with which he extends his voice. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated on the authority of Salamah ibn al-Akwa’ that this embarrassment is for his brother. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9924","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Omar informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Abdul Rahman and Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik told me that Salama bin Al-Akwa’ said: On the Day of Khaybar, my brother fought fiercely with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his sword rebounded on him and killed him. The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about that and doubted it. A man died with his own weapon. Salamah said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived from Khaybar, and I said: O Messenger of God, will you give me permission to stop? For you, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him permission, and Omar said to him: I know what you are saying, so I said: By God, had it not been for God, we would not have been guided nor We gave alms or prayed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You have spoken the truth.” So they sent down tranquility upon us and made our feet firm if we met them. And the polytheists. They transgressed against us, and when I had finished my anger, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who said this?” I said: My brother, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “May God have mercy on him.” I said: O Messenger of God, some people fear praying over him. He said: A man died by his own weapon. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “He died striving and striving.” Ibn Shihab said: Then I asked Ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa’, and he told me, on the authority of his father, similar to that, except that he said: When I said: “People They are afraid to pray for him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They lied. He died as a mujahid, so he will have his reward twice,” and he pointed with his two fingers. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is an error in our opinion, but the correct statement is Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b, on the authority of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, And God knows best. Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Sulayman told us, Ibn Ufayr told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Musafer, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka`b ibn Malik al-Ansari, that Salama ibn al-Akwa’ said: On the Day of Khaybar, my brother fought a fierce battle with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he mentioned something similar to it, and added to it: They said, “Disbelieve.” So we said: “Our father.”"
"9925","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he also told me, meaning Sulayman bin Bilal, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hurairah, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey and he would pray the dawn prayer, he would say: “Everyone who hears hears, praise be to God and His good affliction is upon us. “Our Lord, be our friend and be gracious to us. We seek refuge in God from the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9926","Humayd bin Masada told us, Yazid told us, who is Ibn Zuray’, Sulayman al-Taymi told us, Abu Uthman told us, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, that they were with the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and as they were ascending in a fold, he called out: There is no god but God, and God is great, Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You do not call the deaf or the absent.” Then he said: “Shall I not direct you to a word from the treasure of Paradise?” We said: What is it? He said: “There is no power nor strength except in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9927","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Suwayd, on the authority of Zuhair, Asim Al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, Abu Musa told me, he said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey. When the people overlooked a valley, they loudly shouted “Allahu Akbar” and “Allah is Great” and “Allah is Great, there is no god but Him.” God, and Asim raised his voice, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Be careful with yourselves. Indeed, the one whom you call upon is not deaf. Indeed, he is All-Hearing and Near.” He is with you.” He repeated it three times. Abu Musa said: He heard me say while I was behind him: “There is no power nor strength except in God.” He said: “O Abdullah bin Qais, shall I not tell you a word from the treasures of Paradise? “I said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” He said: “There is no power nor strength except in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9928","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Kathir bin Farqad, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abd God told him that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, retired from the army, or for Hajj or Umrah, he would pay in full or A second time, he says “Allahu Akbar” three times, then says: “There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things.” , Ibon, repentant, worshipers, prostrate, praising our Lord, God has fulfilled His promise, supported His servant, and defeated the parties alone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9929","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, Sufyan told us, Salih bin Kaysan told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, and Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of Ibn Umar, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from Hajj, Umrah, or a campaign, he would pay in full a dime of land. He said: “There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. They are steadfast and repentant. To our Lord we give thanks.” “God fulfilled His promise, supported His servant, and defeated the parties alone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9930","Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Basri told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Jabir said: We were when we were with the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while on a journey, so we ascended and said “Allahu Akbar”, and when we descended we said “Subhaanahu”.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Hasan on the authority of Jabir is a hadith and it is not Hearing (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9931","Muhammad ibn Al-Ala informed us, Ibn Idris informed us, Ahmad ibn Harb informed us, Ibn Fudayl informed us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salem On the authority of Jabir, he said: “When we ascended, we would say ‘Allahu Akbar’, and when we descended, we would say ‘Allahu Akbar’.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9932","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Ayoub bin Sulayman bin Bilal told us, Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Suhail bin Malik, On the authority of his father, he used to listen to the recitation of Omar ibn al-Khattab while he was leading the people in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from my father’s house. Jahm,” and Ka’b al-Ahbar said: “By the One who parted the sea for Moses, because Suhayb told me that Muhammad, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not see a village.” He wants to enter it, but when he sees it, he says: “O God, Lord of the seven heavens and what they have overshadowed, and Lord of the seven earths and what they have reduced, and Lord of the devils and what they have overshadowed.” They have led us astray, by the Lord of the winds and what they have left behind. We ask you for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in you from its evil and the evil of its people and the evil of what is in it.” Ka’b swore by the one who parted the sea to Moses, for these were the supplications of David when he saw the enemy. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9933","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad informed me, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, Hafs ibn Maysarah informed me, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, that Ka’b narrated to him, that Suhayb, the companion of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrated to him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, narrated to him that He, peace and blessings be upon him, never saw a village that he wanted to enter except that he said when he saw it: “O God, Lord of the seven heavens and what they have cast over, and Lord of the earths and what they have diminished. Lord of the devils and what they have led astray, and Lord of the winds and what they create. Indeed, we ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in You from The evil of it, the evil of its people, and the evil of what is in it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hafs bin Maysarah is okay, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad is weak. Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad disagreed with him. Harun bin Abdullah told us, Saad bin Abdul Hamid told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ata Ibn Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Mughith narrated to him, saying: Ka’b said: Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not go to a village wanting Entering it, except that he said when he saw it: It is equal to “the evil of its people.” He said: And Ka’b said: Indeed, Suhayb told him this supplication, on the authority of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Ka’b said: This was the call of David when he saw the enemy. Ibn Ishaq disagreed with him. Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, Al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Mughith bin Amr, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached Khaybar, he said to his companions, while I was among them: “Stand still.” Then he said: “O God, Lord of the heavens and what they overshadow” and something similar, he said: And he used to say it to every town he entered. Zakaria bin Yahya told me, Amr bin Ali told us, Abdullah bin Harun told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, It was narrated to me by someone whom I do not accuse, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Mughith bin Amr, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9934","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, Ibn Jurayj told me, that Abu Al-Zubayr told him, that Ali Al-Asadi told him, That Abdullah bin Omar taught him that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat on his camel while setting out on a journey, he would say “Allahu Akbar” three times and say: “Glory be to Him who has subjected this to us. We would not have been able to do it. Indeed, to our Lord we are turning. Oh God, we ask you on this path of ours.” Righteousness and piety, and of the deeds that You are pleased with, O God, make this journey easy for us, and make it easy for us after it. O God, You are the companion on the journey, And the caliph is in the family. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel, the gloominess of the outlook, and the bad upheavals in family and wealth.” And if He came back and said to them, and added to them: “Repentant, repentant, worshipers, praising our Lord.”"
"9935","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Mansour, Israel, and Fitr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ Ibn Aazib, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from a journey, he would say: “Aibun, repentant, worshipers, praise be to our Lord.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abu Ishaq did not hear it from Al-Bara’."
"9936","Ismail bin Masoud told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Al-Bara’, he heard him He narrates, on the authority of Al-Baraa, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from a journey, he would say: “Aibun, repentant, worshipers, to our Lord.” \They praise\"""""
"9937","Imran bin Musa told us, Abdul-Warith told us, Yahya bin Abi Ishaq told us, Anas bin Malik told us, he said: We were with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, closed his gates in Usfan, and when he overlooked the city, he said: “Aibun, repentant, worshipers, to our Lord, praiseworthy.” He continued saying that until we entered the city."
"9938","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Marhoum bin Abdul Aziz, he is Al-Attar, told us, Abu Naama Al-Saadi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign, and when we stopped, we overlooked Medina. So the people said “Allahu Akbar” and raised their voices with it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: “Indeed, your Lord is neither deaf nor absent. He is among you, at the head of your travels.” Then he said: “O Abdullah bin Qais, shall I not teach you one of the treasures of Paradise? There is no power nor strength except “By God” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9939","Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah told us, Saeed bin Ufayr told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Qais bin Salem, that he heard Abu Umamah bin Sahl, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: We said: O Messenger of God, the people were not afraid when they used to say, “When Supervise the city: provide us with sustenance and stability therein? He said: “They feared the injustice of the rulers and the drought of rain.”"
"9940","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, Suwayd told us, Abdullah told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, is similar to the fact that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If an animal stumbles upon you, do not say: Unfortunate.” Satan, it grows until it becomes like a house, and he says: I made it by my power, but say: In the name of God. Then it grows smaller until it becomes \like flies\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9941","Othman bin Abdullah told me, Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Muhammad bin Hamran Al-Qaisi told us, Khaled Al-Hadha’ told us, about Abu Tamimah Al-Hujaimi, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, said: I was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and our camel stumbled, so I said: Satan was miserable, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not say: Satan is miserable, for he will become great until he becomes like a house and says: By my power. But say: In the name of God, for he will become as small as a fly.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: What is correct in our opinion is the hadith of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, but in my opinion this is an error. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abd al-Wahhab told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Tamimah, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, he said: He was a common man. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was riding his animal, and his animal tripped over him, and the man said: Miserable Satan, the same is sent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9942","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told me, Asad bin Musa told us, Aafiya bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Hashimi, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking and a woman was in front of him, I said: The path is for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And she said, “The path is obstructive. If He wishes, He may turn to the right, and if He wishes, He may take the left.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave her, for she is a mighty one.” I said: It is it. He said: “It is in the heart.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Aafia bin Yazid is trustworthy, and Suleiman Al-Hashimi I do not know him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9943","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Sa`id bin Yasar Abi al-Hubab, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid, on the authority of Abu Talha, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Angels do not enter a house in which there are dogs or statues.” So I said: Go. We went to Aisha to ask her about that. We went to her and said: O mother, this man told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No.” “The angels enter a house in which there is a dog and no statue.” Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention that? She said: No, but I will tell you what I saw him do. He went out on some of his raids, and I was waiting for him to arrive, so I took a pattern and covered it. When he came, I met him at the door and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God and God’s mercy. Praise be to God who has honored you, helped you, and honored you. The chain of the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9944","Amr bin Mansour told us, Abu Nu`aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, he said: I heard a grasshopper, saying: While The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking, when a stone hit him and he stumbled, and his finger was bloodied. He said: Are you anything but a finger? You have been bloodied, and in the cause of God I will not die. \You found\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9945","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yaqoub, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah On the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Khawla bint Hakim Al-Sulamiyah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Whoever stays at one place and then says: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created, nothing will harm him until he departs from that place of his.” Ibn Ajlan disagreed with him"
"9946","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, Hibban told us, Wahib told us, Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad bin Malik, on the authority of Khawla, daughter of Hakim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If When one of you stays in a house, he says: I seek refuge in the words of God from the evil of what He has created. Nothing will harm him in that house until he leaves it. Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad told us, Mukhlid told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9947","Issa bin Hammad told us, Al-Layth told me, Bukayr told me, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, and Busr bin Saeed, they said: A man came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Did a scorpion sting me? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “But if you had said in the evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, from the evil of what He created, it would not have harmed you.”"
"9948","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Baqiya told us, Safwan bin Amr told us, he said: Shuraih bin Ubaid told me, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was traveling and the night came, he would say: “O land, my Lord And your Lord is God, I seek refuge in God from your evil, from the evil of what is within you, from the evil of what He created in you, from the evil of what crawls upon you, I seek refuge in you from lions and lions, Of the serpent and the scorpion, and of the inhabitant of the land, and of his father and his father.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Al-Zubayr bin Al-Walid is a Syrian. I do not know of him except this hadith."
"9949","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, Abd al-Ala told us, Wahib told us, Suhail told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he used to say when morning came: “O God, by you we have entered the morning, by you we have entered the evening, by you we live, and by you we die. And to You is the resurrection.” And when evening came, he said: “With You we have entered the evening, and with You we have entered the morning, and with You we live, and with You we will die, and to You is the resurrection.” He said: And once again: “And to you is the final destination.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9950","Ali bin Khashram told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Bilal, on the authority of Sabiq bin Najiya, on the authority of Abu Salam, he said: A man passed by us. Long and disheveled, it was said: This served the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I got up to him and said: Did you serve the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, I said: Tell me about him a hadith that the men did not circulate between you and him. He said: I heard him say: “Whoever said in the morning and in the evening three Several times: I was satisfied with God as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, and with Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as a Prophet. It was God’s duty to please him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9951","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Ubadah. He is Ibn Muslim. Jubayr bin Abi Sulayman bin told me. Jubayr bin Mutim said that he was sitting with Ibn Umar, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in his supplication in the evening and when It becomes: “Oh God, I ask you for well-being in this world and the hereafter, O God, I ask you for forgiveness and well-being, in my religion and in my world, And my family, and my money, O God, cover my private parts, and secure my beauty, O God, protect me from before me, and from behind me, and from my right, and from my left, and from Above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness lest I be attacked from under me.” Jubayr said: It is an eclipse. Ubadah said: I do not know what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Say hello or say “Jabir”? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9952","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Abu Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that Abu Bakr was satisfied By God, he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Tell me some words to say in the morning and in the evening? He said: He said: “O God, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself and the evil of Satan,” and he said: “Say it in the morning, and in the evening, and when you come, and when you go to bed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9953","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, Ibn Abi Al-Shawareb told us, Abdul Aziz bin Al-Mukhtar told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says in the morning and in the evening: Glory be to God And by praising Him a hundred times, no one brought anything better than what he brought except one who said the same as what he said or added to it.”"
"9954","Ubayd Allah bin Faddala told me, Abdullah told us, Saeed told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman bin Hujayra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Sulayman al-Khair and said: “Indeed The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wants to give you words that you will ask the Most Gracious, and that you will desire from Him day and night, saying: Oh God. I ask you for health in faith, faith in good character, success followed by success, mercy from you and well-being, and forgiveness and satisfaction from you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9955","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Othman bin Muhib Al-Hashimi told me, I heard Anas bin Malik said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Fatima: “What is preventing you from listening to what I advise you to do, or saying in the morning and when \O evening"," O Ever-Living"," O Ever-Subsisting"," by Your mercy I seek help. Reconcile all my affairs for me"," and do not leave me to myself for the blink of an eye.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9956","Muawiyah bin Salih told us, Mansour, who is Ibn Abi Muzahim, told us, Abu Al-Muhyah Yahya bin Ya’la told us, on the authority of Mansour On the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir Al-Bajli, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “When one of you wakes up in the morning, let him say: I praise you in the morning, praise be to you, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, three times.” And when the evening comes, let him say: \Like that\"""""
"9957","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abu Amir told us, Abd al-Jalil told us, Ja`far bin Maimun told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi told me Tomorrow, he said to his father: O Father, I hear you praying every morning: “O God, grant me health in my body, O God, grant me health in my hearing, O God, grant me health in my sight.” “There is no god but You.” She repeats it three times in the morning and three times in the evening, and says: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the grave. There is no god but You.” Do you repeat it three times in the morning, and three times in the evening? He said: Yes, my son, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicating for them, so I would like to follow his Sunnah. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ja`far ibn Maimun is not strong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9958","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Abdul Wahid told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, Ibrahim bin Suwayd Al-Nakha’i told us, he told us Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: When the evening came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would say: “Our evening And the kingdom belongs to God, and praise be to God, and there is no god but God, He alone, with no partner.” Al-Hasan said: Al-Zubaidi told me that he was narrated on the authority of Abraham in this: “To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things, O God.” I ask You for the good of this night, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of this night and the evil of what comes after it. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from laziness. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the Fire and the torment of the grave.” Salamah bin Kuhayl disagreed with him and stopped him."
"9959","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, Muhammad told us, and Shu’bah mentioned, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, that he used to command us, in the morning and in the evening, to say: “There is no god but God, alone.” He has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise. We have entered the morning and dominion belongs to God. O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of this day, and from the evil of what after him, and I seek refuge in You from laziness, bad arrogance, the torment of the grave, and the torment of the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9960","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: I told Ubayd Allah bin Muadh and I read it to him, your father told you, Shu’bah told us about the ruling. On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God, alone A partner to Him, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things a hundred times in the morning, and a hundred times in the evening, and no one comes. “Better than that, except for those who say better than that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9961","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, Abd al-A’la told us, Dawud told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God, He alone has no partner, His is the dominion and His is praise, and He is over everything.” Almighty, two hundred times, and no one will ever catch up with him after him, except he who said the same as what he said or better.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9962","Amr bin Mansour and Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, Al-Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, And Dawud, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says on a day two hundred Once: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. No one before Him has preceded Him. And no one after him will achieve it except those who did better than his work.”"
"9963","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Al-Jallah Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Hubali, on the authority of Amara bin Shabib Al-Sabai’i said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says: There is no god but God, He alone has no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. He will die, and He has power over all things. Ten times after sunset, God will send him a weapon to protect him from Satan until the morning. “And ten positive good deeds were recorded for him, and ten fatal sins were erased from him, and it was for him as the equivalent of ten believing slaves.” Amr bin Al-Harith disagreed with him"
"9964","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, that Al-Jallah told him, That Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Maafiri narrated to him, that Ammar al-Sabai narrated to him, that a man from the Ansar narrated to him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to him And peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever says after sunset or dawn: There is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. He gives life and causes death. And He is Able to do all things. Ten times, God has sent him armed men to guard him until morning, and from the time of morning until evening, “similar to it.”"
"9965","Abdah bin Abdullah, I am Suwayd, told us on the authority of Zuhayr, who is the son of Muawiyah, Al-Walid bin Tha’labah told us, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says between the morning and the evening and dies on that day or night will enter Paradise, whoever says: Oh God, you are my Lord, there is no god but You, you created me and I am your servant, and I abide by your covenant and promise as much as I am able, I seek refuge I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I seek refuge in Your grace, and I seek refuge in my sin, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except You.”"
"9966","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Bashir bin Ka’b On the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The master of seeking forgiveness is to say: O God, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I acknowledge Your grace and I acknowledge My sin. So forgive me. No one forgives sins except you. If he says them in the morning and is certain of them, and then dies, he will be among the people of Paradise, even if he says them after the evening. Being certain of it, then he died. He was one of the people of Paradise.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Husayn is more reliable in our view than Al-Walid ibn Tha’labah, and he is more knowledgeable about Abdullah ibn Buraidah, and his hadith is better. Correctly (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9967","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, Yazid told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, and Abu al-Awwam, On the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, that people from the people of Kufa were on a journey and with them was Shaddad bin Aws. They said to him: Speak to us, may God have mercy on you. He said: Bring me a scroll and an inkwell. They brought him a scroll and an inkwell, and he said: Write: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Who said In the morning and in the evening: Oh God, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I seek refuge in You for your blessing upon me, and I seek refuge in You for my sin, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except You. If he says it in the morning and dies that day, he will be forgiven and will be admitted to Paradise, and if he says it in the evening and dies that night, he will be forgiven and admitted. Paradise (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9968","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The man should not say: O God, forgive me if You wish, O God, have mercy on me if You wish, but rather to resolve the issue.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9969","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “None of you should say: O God, forgive me if you wish, but let him resolve the issue, for God Almighty does not I hate it” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9970","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Ismail informed us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When one of you supplicates, let him be determined to ask, and do not say: Give me if you wish, for God does not deprive him of it.”"
"9971","Issa bin Hammad informed us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Yaqub, that it was mentioned to him that Abu Salih He told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said to him: I was stung by a scorpion, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If you had said in the evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created, it would not have harmed you.”"
"9972","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Al-Layth informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Yaqoub Ibn Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I was stung by a scorpion. He said: “As for If you had said: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He created, it would not have harmed you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9973","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, And his father, Al-Harith bin Yaqoub. Ya’qub bin Abdullah said, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I did not meet a scorpion that stung me yesterday. He said: But if you had said in the evening: I seek refuge With the perfect words of God, from the evil of what He created, it will not harm you.”"
"9974","I read about Muhammad bin Sulaiman Luwayn, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man from The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was bitten, and what God wished was achieved from him. Then that reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “If He said: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He created, it would not harm Him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9975","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man from Islam said: I did not sleep. This night, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “From what?” He said: I was stung by a scorpion. He said: “But if you had said when Evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created. Nothing will harm you, God willing."
"9976","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says in the evening three times: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created will not The sting of that night would harm him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9977","Muhammad bin Othman Al-Uqaili told us, saying: Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was absent from him one night, so he asked about him, and when the morning came, he came to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “What imprisoned you?” He said: O Messenger of God, I was stung by a scorpion. He said: “If you had said in the evening: I seek refuge in the words of “Allah will protect you from the evil of what He created three times, and He will not harm you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9978","Ibrahim bin Yusuf al-Kufi told us, and he is not strong, he said: Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, said: A man was stung by a scorpion, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and told him, and he said: “But if you had said when “I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created, so that nothing will harm you.” This Ibrahim bin Yusuf al-Kufi is not strong in hadith, and Ibrahim bin Yusuf al-Balkhi is trustworthy. Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from Islam, Like it. Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from He became Muslim. He said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man from his companions came and said: I was stung yesterday, like him. Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from Islam, who said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then a man from the Ansar came to him and said at the end: “If God wills.” Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suhail and his brother, on the authority of their father, on the authority of a man Whoever became Muslim was bitten, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to do the same. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salih , sent (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9979","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Marwazi told me, he said: Yaqoub told us, he said: My nephew Ibn Shihab told us, on the authority of his uncle, he said: He told me Tariq bin Makhashin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that a stinging person was brought, and he said: “If only he had said: I seek refuge in the words of God is free from the evil of what He created. He is neither stung nor harmed.” Kathir ibn Ubaid told me, he said: Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Tariq ibn Makhashin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the same. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Al-Zubaidi is more steadfast than my nephew Al-Zuhri, and my nephew Al-Zuhri is not With that strong man, he has no objectionable hadith on the authority of Al-Zuhri. Yunus disagreed with him. He said: Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, we were informed that Abu Hurairah, Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9980","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Abdullah bin Qays. That his father told him that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was afraid of a people, he would say: “O God, we place you in their presence, and we seek refuge in you from \Their evils\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9981","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the Day of the Trench, says: “O God, who sends down the Book, who is quick to judge, who moves the clouds, defeat them and shake them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9982","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn On the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “These were the last words of Abraham, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was thrown into the Fire. God suffices me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.” He said: And your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something like it: Those to whom the people said, “The people have gathered against you, so fear them,” and it increased their faith. And they said, “Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9983","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Azhar bin al-Qasim told us, he said: Al-Muthanna bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, he said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, invaded, he would say: “O God, you are my support and my helper, and by you I fight.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9984","Abdah bin Abdullah, I am Suwayd, told us, on the authority of Zuhayr, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Bara, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, that Abu Sufyan bin Al-Harith was leading him on the day of Hunayn while he was riding his white mule, so he dismounted, then asked for victory, then he said: “ I am the Prophet, no lie, I am Ibn Abdul Muttalib.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9985","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Omar bin Hafs told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq On the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When we met on the day of Badr, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to pray, and I did not see anyone seeking He seeks a truth that is stronger than the appeal of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, to his Lord Almighty, and he says: “O God, I seek Your promise and your covenant, Oh God, I ask you for what you promised me, O God, if this group is destroyed, it will not be worshiped on earth.” Then he turned to us as if his face was split by the moon. Then he said: “These are the people’s evening skies.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9986","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Amr bin Murrah, he said: Abdullah bin told me. Al-Harith, who said: Taliq ibn Qays told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray with this supplication: “My Lord, help me.” And do not help me, and support me, and do not support me, and plot against me, and do not plot against me, and guide me and facilitate guidance for me, and help me against him who transgresses against me, my Lord. Make me grateful to You, remembrance of You, fearful of You, obedient to You, loving to You, sincere and repentant to You, my Lord, accept my repentance, and wash Support me, confirm my proof, guide my heart, guide my tongue, and remove the weakness of my heart.” Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahadah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray: “Lord, help me.” He narrated the hadith mursal, the hadith of Sufyan is preserved, and Yahya bin Saeed said: I have not seen anyone with a better memory than Sufyan, and it was narrated on the authority of Al-Thawri that he He said: I have never entrusted anything to my heart and it has betrayed me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9987","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ayman told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Rifa’ah. Al-Zarqi, on the authority of his father, said: When it was the day of Uhud, the polytheists retreated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Prepare until I praise... “My Lord,” so they formed in rows behind him, and he said: “O God, all praise is due to You. There is no one to seize what You have spread, nor to extend what You have taken, and there is no guide to whom. You have led astray, and there is no one who misleads whom You have guided, and there is no giver of what You have withheld, and there is no deterrence of what You have given, and there is no bringer of what You have distanced, and no one can turn away from what You have brought near, O God. Extend upon us your blessings, your mercy, your grace, and your provision. Oh God, I ask you for the ever-lasting bliss that does not change or fade away. Oh God, I I ask You for bliss on the day of family, and security on the day of fear. Oh God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have given us and the evil of what You have withheld from us. Oh God, make us beloved. Faith, and beautify it in our hearts, and make disbelief, immorality, and disobedience amiss to us, and make us among the rightly guided, O God, let us die as Muslims, And give us life as Muslims, and join us with the righteous, not disgraced or tempted. O God, kill the infidels who deny Your messengers and turn away from Your path, and inflict upon them Your punishment and torment, O God of truth, Amen.” Abu Nu`aym disagreed with him and sent the hadith. Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Abdul-Wahid bin Ayman told us, he said: I heard Ubaid bin Rifa’ah Al-Zarqi said: When it was the day of Uhud, he mentioned something similar to it."
"9988","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Majeed al-Hanafi told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Gifted, on the authority of Ismail bin Aoun bin Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali bin Abi Talib, On the authority of his father, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali, on the authority of Ali, he said: On the day of Badr, I fought some of the fighting, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, I saw what he had done, so I came and saw him prostrating, saying: “O Living, O Ever-Living, O Ever-Living, O Ever-Subsisting.” Then I returned to The fight, then I came, and he was prostrating, nothing more than that. Then I went to the fight, then I came, and he was prostrating, saying that. So God granted him victory (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9989","Muhammad bin Aqeel told us, he said: Hafs told us, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray: “O Living, O Sustaining.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9990","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, he said: It was part of the supplication of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “Either Living, Eternal” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9991","Muhammad bin Uthman told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Sulayman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila On the authority of Suhayb, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed, he would whisper something and would not tell us about it. He said: “Have you informed me?” They said: Yes. He said: “I mentioned one of the prophets who was given soldiers from his people, and he said: Who will reward these or stand up for them?” Solomon said a similar word. With this, it was said to him: Choose for your people between one of three: between me attacking them with an enemy from other than them, or hunger, or death, so they said You are the Prophet of God. All of this is up to you, so be proud of us. He said in his prayer, and when they began to pray, he said: As for an enemy other than them, no. As for famine, not death, but death was imposed on them for three days, and seventy thousand died. What you see is that I say: My Lord, through you I fight. And with You I make my foundations, and there is no power or strength except with You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9992","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Baraa, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “You will meet your enemy tomorrow, so let your slogan be (Ham): Do not support the call of your Prophet.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9993","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Al-Ajlah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You will meet the enemy tomorrow, and your slogan is (Ham) they will not be helped.” Al-Ajlah was not strong and was excessive in his Shiism. Zuhair and Sharik differed from them in the chain of transmission and wording, despite their differences in it."
"9994","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Safra, he said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to me. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the night of the ditch: “I do not see people except “May you spend the night, for your slogan is (Ham) and they will not be helped.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9995","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Safra He said: He was afraid that he would spend the night. Al-Haruriyya: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, dug the ditch and he was afraid that Abu Sufyan: “If you stay overnight, then indeed your claim (Ham) will not be helped.”"
"9996","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad ibn Amr informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, and he mentioned Another before him, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, said: When it was the day of Uhud and the people turned away, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He greeted twelve men from the Ansar, and among them was Talha bin Ubayd Allah. The polytheists overtook him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to him. And he said: “Who are the people?” Talha said: “I am.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As you are.” A man from the Ansar said: “I am.” O Messenger of God, so he said: “You.” He fought until he was killed, then he turned around, and behold, he was among the polytheists. He said: “Who is for the people?” So Talha said: I, he said: “As you are.” Then a man from the Ansar said: I, so he said: “You.” So he fought like his companion until he was killed, then he continued to say That is when a man from the Ansar would go out to them and fight like those before him until he was killed, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Talha remained. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who is for the people?” Talha said: I am. So he fought like the eleven men, until his hand was struck and cut off. He touched his fingers and said: He felt. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you had said: In the name of God, the angels would have exalted you while the people were watching. Then God turned back the polytheists.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9997","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Jundub bin Sufyan, he said: A human being The finger of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in some battles. He said: “Are you anything but a finger? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9998","Qutayba bin Saeed and Sulayman bin Mansour told us, and the wording is his, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A strong believer is better and more beloved to God than a weak believer, and in everything there is good. Strive for what will benefit you, and do not be incapable of it. If something overwhelms you, say: God has decreed and what God wills, and beware of law, for law opens up work. \Satan\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"9999","Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Al-Basri told us, Al-Fudayl, who is Ibn Sulaiman, told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ajlan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A strong believer is better and more beloved to God than a weak believer. Strive for what will benefit you, and do not be weary. If something overwhelms you, say: God has decreed, and He has done what He wills. Beware of temptation, for temptation opens work. Satan.” Al-Fudayl bin Suleiman is not strong. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10000","Al-Hasan bin Ahmad told us, he said: Abdullah, who is the son of Muhammad bin Asma, told us, he said: Abdullah, who is the son of Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The believer A strong person is better and more preferable in the sight of God than a weak believer, and in everything there is good. Strive for what will benefit you and do not fail. If a matter overwhelms you, say: It is decreed. God does what He wills, and beware of the sound of God, for the sound opens the work of Satan.” Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of al-Araj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So he mentioned something like it. Abdullah said: I heard it from Rabi’ah, and I have memorized it. From Muhammad (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10001","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Idris informed us, he said: Rabi’ah bin Uthman informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban. On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A strong believer is better and more beloved to God than a weak believer.” And everything in it is good. Strive for what will benefit you, and seek help from God and do not fail. If something happens to you, do not say: If only I had done such-and-such. And such and such, but say: God has decreed and whatever He wills He does. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10002","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Saif, on the authority of Awf bin Malik that he told them, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, judged between two men, and the one who was judged said: God suffices me, and He is the best disposer of affairs. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Return the man to me.” He said: “What did you say?” He said: I said: God suffices me, and He is the best disposer of affairs. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed God blames you for your inability, but you have to be wise, and if you are overcome by a matter, say: God suffices me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: A sword I do not know. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10003","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Aban bin Saleh, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, he said: Ibn Ja’far used to say: My father taught me, meaning Ali. His mother was under Ali. He said: Teach me some words that he claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught him. He used them to say them when he was in distress. He came down with it and said: My sons, I have spared them from Hasan and Husayn and have allocated them to you. We used to ask him about them and he would conceal them, but he refused. To teach them, until he married his daughter in marriage and we went out to mourn her, until when we were in labor and she was riding and he left her, he went alone with her while she was riding her animal. So I knew that he was teaching her those words that he used to keep secret, then he left her and we left, until when we walked close to a mile away, I fell behind. It was as if I was spilling water, then I ran and said: Oh cousin, I know that your father left you alone to teach you the words that were He keeps us secret. She said: Yes. I said: Tell me about them. She said: He has forbidden me from telling anyone about them. I said: I ask you by God except what You told me, perhaps I will never see you after this situation. She said: He was alone with me. Then he said to me: Yes, my daughter. My father taught me some words that he taught him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used them to say when distress befell him, and said: I have allocated you with them instead of Hasan and Hussein, and you are When you approach a land to which you are a stranger, then if distress befalls you, or distress befalls you, say to them: “There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to You, Blessed be God, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10004","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: my uncle told us, he said: my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: he told me Aban bin Saleh, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of the daughter of Abdullah bin Ja’far, who was with Abdul Al-Malik bin Marwan, on the authority of her father, Abdullah bin Ja’far, Ali said: Abdullah bin Ja’far used to say: My father Ali bin taught me Abu Talib, there are some words that I say when I am in distress, and he says: Oh my sons, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught them to me. I say them when When distress befalls me, I have allocated them to you rather than Hasan and Husayn. He said: Ibn Ja`far used to keep them a secret, so when he married that daughter of his, Abd The king and she headed to the Levant. He took her on her way and we took her on his way with him. When she took her leave and he wanted to leave, he was alone with her, and we knew that he was teaching her. So when he left, I lagged behind, then I caught up with her and asked her, and he said: And he mentioned a word that meant it. He said to me: Yes, my daughter, you are coming forward. A land to which you are a stranger, so if distress or distress befalls you, say these words: “There is no god but Allah, the Most Generous, the Most Forbearing, blessed be God.” Lord of the Great Throne, praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” Aban bin Salih said, and Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Had, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far Like them (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10005","Ubayd Allah ibn Saad narrated to us, he said: My uncle narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Aban bin Salih narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught me May God bless him and grant him peace. Words I say when distress befalls me. I have not taught them good or good, nor Husayn. I have chosen them for you when something troubles you. So say: “There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to Him, blessed be God, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10006","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hadi On the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, on the authority of Ali, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met me with these words, and commanded me to reveal them to me. Anguish or distress for me to say: “There is no god but God, the Generous, the Forbearing. Glory be to Him. Blessed be God, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the Throne.” \ So Abdullah bin Jaafar used to teach it to the dead"," and he would breathe it on the sick"," and he would teach it to the expatriate of his daughters. (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"10007","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ismail bin Ubaid bin Abi Karimah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Abd Al-Rahim, on the authority of Abdul-Wahhab bin Bakht, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Hadi, on the authority of Abdul Allah bin Jafar, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught him these words to say On the sick person: “There is no god but God, the Most Gracious, the Forbearing. Glory be to God. Blessed be God, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10008","Yahya bin Uthman told us, he said: Zayd bin Yahya bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abu Thuban, he said: Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr told me, He heard Muhammad bin Ajlan speaking, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far bin Abi Talib, on the authority of some of his family, On the authority of Ja’far bin Abi Talib, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught him words that when distress befell him, he supplicated them: “There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous.” “Glory be to God, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” This is a mistake, and Abu Thuban is weak and no argument like him can be supported. The correct thing is the hadith of Ya’qub. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10009","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i bin Harash, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Shaddad Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Jafar, said: Ali said to me: I will inform you of words that I did not inform Hasan or Hussein. If you ask God a question and you would like to succeed, say: “There is no god but God. He alone has no partner. He is the Most High, the Great. There is no god but God. Alone, He has no partner, the Most Forbearing, the Most Generous.”"
"10010","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaddad Ibn Al-Had, that Ali said to his nephew: If you ask God and want to succeed, say: “There is no god but God, alone, without any partner.” To Him belongs the Most High, the Great, there is no god but Allah, He alone has no partner, He is the Most Forbearing, the Most Generous.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10011","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad. On the authority of Ali, that he said to Ibn Jafar: Shall I not narrate to you a speech that neither Al-Hasan nor Al-Hussein narrate to you, when you ask God for a need and you want to They succeeded, so they said: “There is no god but Allah, Alone, with no partner, the Forbearing, the Generous. There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, the Most High, the Great.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10012","Safwan bin Amr told me, he said: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, he said: “The words of relief: There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great, there is no god but Allah, the Most Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Great Throne, and praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” Khalaf bin Tamim disagreed with him in his chain of transmission and in his wording."
"10013","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told me, he said: Khalaf bin Tamim told us, he said: Israel told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not teach you some words that if you say them, may God forgive you for Indeed, you are forgiven. There is no god but God, the Most High, the Great. There is no god but Him, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the Magnificent Throne. Praise be to God. Lord of the worlds.” Ali bin Saleh and Yusuf bin Ishaq bin Abi Ishaq disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10014","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr told us, he said: Ali bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Shall I not teach you? Words that if you say them, you will be forgiven even though you are forgiven. There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great. Glory be to God, Lord. The seven heavens and the Lord of the Great Throne, praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.” Ahmad bin Uthman told us, he said: Shuraih bin Maslamah told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and something similar. Al-Hussein bin Waqid disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10015","Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not teach you a supplication that if you pray with it, God will forgive you, and if you are forgiven?” I said: Yes, He said: “There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great, there is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Most Generous, there is no god but Allah, Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Great Throne.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10016","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Jaafar told me, he said: Asim bin Al-Nadr told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Mis'ar told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, on the authority of Hassan ibn Hassan, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ja'far, he said regarding these words: “There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the Great Throne. Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds. O God, forgive me. O God, have mercy on me. Oh God, forgive me, O God, forgive me.” Abdullah bin Jafar said: My uncle told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught him These words (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10017","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Mas’ar told us On the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hassan, that Abdullah bin Jaafar came to see a sick son of his, called Saleh, and said: “Say: There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Most Generous. Glory be to God, Lord of the Great Throne. O God, forgive me. O God, have mercy on me. O God, forgive me. O God, forgive me, for You are pardoning and forgiving.” Then he said: These words were taught to me by my uncle. He mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught them to them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10018","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Rafi’ told us, On the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, he married his daughter to Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf, and he said to her: “When he consumms the sexual intercourse with you, say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing.” The Generous, Glory be to God, Lord of the Great Throne, praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds.” He claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would say this when his party was upset."
"10019","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Amr bin Othman told me, he said: Muhammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar, on the authority of Abu Hilal said this: on the authority of. . Abu Abd al-Rahman said: His saying: on the authority of Abu Hilal is a mistake, but he is Hilal and he is a loyalist of them. He said: on the authority of Omar ibn Abd Al-Aziz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, on the authority of Asma’ bint Umays, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught her words to say when Anguish: “God, God, my Lord, I do not associate anything with Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10020","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar, on the authority of Hilal, On the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught him when he was in distress: God, God, my Lord. I do not associate anything with Him.” This is a mistake, but the correct thing is the hadith of Abu Nu’aym (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10021","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar told us, on the authority of Hilal, the client of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: My mother, Asma’ bint Umays, taught me something. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to You say it when you are in distress: “God is God, my Lord, and I do not associate anything with Him.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is correct."
"10022","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered his family, and said: “If the If any of you is distressed or sad, let him say seven times: “Allah is my Lord, I do not associate anything with Him.”"
"10023","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Amer told us, he said: Abdul Jalil bin Atiya told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Maymun, He said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The supplications of the distressed: Oh God I hope for your mercy, so do not leave me to myself for the blink of an eye, and set all my affairs straight for me. There is no god but You.”"
"10024","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would say: “No.” There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Great, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Great Throne, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne, there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Heavens And the Lord of the Earth, the Lord of the Great Throne.” Then he calls"
"10025","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Sa’id and Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abi Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to supplicate them during times of distress: “There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Great. There is no god but God, Lord of the Heavens and Lord of the Earth, Lord of the Noble Throne.” Mahdi bin Maymun disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10026","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Mahdi ibn Maimun, he said: Yusuf ibn Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: Abu Al-Aaliyah said to me: Shall I not teach you a supplication that I was informed of, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was when it was revealed With the intensity of his supplication: “There is no god but God, the Great, the Forbearing, there is no god but God, Lord of the Great Throne, there is no god but God, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, Lord of the Earth.” “The Noble Throne” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10027","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria told us, he said: Ubaid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Muhammad bin Muhajir told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin told me. Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Shall I not tell you, or speak to you? What if distress or affliction from this world befalls a man among you and he supplicates for it and he will be relieved? It was said to him: Yes. He said: The supplication of Dhul-Nun: There is no god but Him. Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10028","Humayd bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The supplication of Dhul-Nun when he supplicated with it while he was in the belly of the whale: No.” There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers, for no Muslim will ever supplicate with it for anything but his prayer will be answered.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10029","Abdul Rahman bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Sahl bin Hashim, he said: Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Thawban, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, meant something, he would say: “Allah is Allah, my Lord, He has no partner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10030","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Abu Ja`far told us, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah, On the authority of Uthman bin Hanif, that a blind man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I am a blind man, so pray to God To heal me, he said: “Rather, I pray to you.” He said: Pray to God for me, two or three times. He said: “Perform ablution, then pray two rak’ahs, then say: Oh God, I I ask you and I turn to you through my Prophet Muhammad, the Prophet of mercy. O Muhammad, I turn to God through you to fulfill my need, or my need to “So-and-so, or my need for such-and-such, O God, make my Prophet intercede on my behalf, and grant me intercession on my own behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10031","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Uthman bin Omar told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah bin Thabit, on the authority of Uthman bin Hunaif, that a blind man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I pray to God Almighty to grant me health. He said: If you wish, you may supplicate, and if you wish, you may be patient, for that is better for you.” He said: “Call him.” He ordered him to perform his ablution and perform his ablution well, and to supplicate with this. Supplication: “Oh God, I ask you, and I turn to you through your prophet Muhammad, the prophet of mercy. Indeed, I turned to you to my Lord in this need of mine.” So judge for me, O God, make him intercede on my behalf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10032","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of my father Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, on the authority of his uncle, that a blind man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, pray May God reveal to me my sight. He said: “Should I leave you?” He said: O Messenger of God, it is difficult for me to lose my sight. He said: “So go and perform ablution. Then pray two rak'ahs, then say: Oh God, I ask you and I turn to you through my Prophet Muhammad, the Prophet of mercy, O Muhammad, I turn to you to May your Lord reveal to me my sight, grant him intercession for me, and grant me intercession for myself.” So he returned and had revealed his sight to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10033","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Harun bin Abi Issa, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibn Ishaq told me. And Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He told me Utbah bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: People are about to question each other until someone says: This is God who created creation, so who created God? So if they say that, then say: God is One? { 1 } God is the Eternal, the Eternal. { 2 } He neither begot nor was generated. { 3 } And there is no one equal to Him. { 4 } Then let him spit to his left three times, and seek refuge in God from Satan.” Amr said: Then let him spit on his left three times and seek refuge from Satan."
"10034","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Satan comes to one of you and says: Who...? So whoever finds any of that, let him say: I believe in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10035","Harun bin Saeed told us, he said: Khalid bin Nizar told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Mabrur told me, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Urwah said: Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The servant comes and says: Who created such-and-such? Who created such-and-such? “If that happens, let him seek refuge in God and let him finish.”"
"10036","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Some of the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: We find within ourselves something that we find it difficult to speak? He said: “Have you found him?” They said: Yes. He said: “That is clear faith.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10037","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, regarding a man who finds in himself something that he does not like to talk about, he said: “That is pure faith.”"
"10038","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Abraham, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “That is pure faith.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10039","Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yusuf, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas That a man came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: I find in myself something that, because I am a lava, would I like to speak about? Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God is great. Praise be to God, who turned his machinations into obsessive thoughts.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I did not know that anyone followed Isaac on this narration, and what is correct is what Abd al-Rahman narrated. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10040","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Al-Amash, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Abdul Allah Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of God, I find in myself something that is more beloved to me than to be a dove. Did he speak it? So he said in the hadith of Mansour: “God is the greatest,” and they all said: “Praise be to God who reduced his matter to whispering.”"
"10041","Mahmoud ibn Ghaylan informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of Mansour and Al-A’mash, they heard Dharr ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of God, one of us finds something to be a beloved dove. Who should he speak to? One of them said: “Praise be to God, who has not given you anything except obsessiveness,” and the other said: “Praise be to God, who has reduced his affairs to obsessiveness.”"
"10042","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Al-Awam told us, he said: Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani told me, on the authority of Suleiman bin Surad On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, that two men were brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had differed regarding the recitation, each of them claiming that the Prophet had prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He recited it. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it to them, but they disagreed. He said to them: “You have done well.” My father said: Then I was filled with more doubt than I had been in during pre-Islamic times, so I said: You have done well, you have done well. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck. He held my chest in his hand, then he said: “O God, remove the devil from him.” He said: Then I dropped a sweat, as if I was looking at God with a difference. Then he said: “ Indeed, I have been commanded to recite the Qur’an in seven harfs.” Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sulayman bin Surad He said: Ubayy bin Ka’b, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to two men who disagreed about the recitation, something like this. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10043","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amara bin Abi Hassan Al-Mazini, On the authority of his uncle, that people asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the obsession that one of them experiences, causing him to fall from the chandelier. Is it more beloved to him than to speak about it? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He is a man of clear faith. Indeed, Satan comes to the servant with anything less than that, and if he is protected from it, he falls into \There\"""""
"10044","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: “Say: He is Allah, the One who is just.” a third of the Qur’an”"
"10045","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Bakr told us, he said: Abu Husayn told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “Whoever recites Say, He is God, One has read a third of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10046","Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Abdul-Azeem told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Muadh, he said: My father told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Is any of you incapable of To recite a third of the Qur’an every night? He said: Who can bear that? He said: “Yes, say: He is God, One.” It was narrated by Suleiman Al-Amash, on the authority of Abraham, so he sent it. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, sent. Muhammad ibn Al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: A messenger (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10047","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of a woman, From the Ansar, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Qur’an every night?” “So we remained silent, and he repeated his words to us three times and we remained silent, then he said: “Whoever recites Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad in the night has recited a third of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10048","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, On the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of a woman, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Say, ‘He is Allah, One and One-third of the Qur’an.’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10049","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Zaida told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Rabi’ bin Khathim, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of a woman, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Say He is God, one third of the Qur’an.” I do not know of an authentic hadith longer than this. Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, and Yusuf bin Marwan told us, they said: Fudayl bin Iyad told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Khathim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of a woman, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10050","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Bishr bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abdul Samad told us, he said: he told us Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of a woman, from the Ansar, that Abu Ayyub He told her, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites: Say, He is God, One, in the night, has read a third of the Qur’an.” This is wrong"
"10051","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal, he said: It was spring. When he sits, he does not get up until he narrates these two hadiths, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, and a hadith that he refers to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Between them was a woman. He said: “Say: He is Allah, One. It is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10052","Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, that a man from the Ansar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites Say, He is God, One It is as if he had recited a third of the Qur’an.”"
"10053","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, On the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever recites: Say, He is God, One, it is as if he has recited a third of the Qur’an.”"
"10054","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Ali told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari said: “Say, ‘He is Allah, One’. It is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an.”"
"10055","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, that Abu Ayyub said: “Say: He is God, one of God, the eternal, one-third of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10056","Ali bin Saeed bin Masruq Al-Kufi told us, he said: Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, He said: Some of Muhammad’s companions, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Say: He is God, one third of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10057","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, he said: The Prophet said, May God bless him and grant him peace: “Say, ‘He is God, One.’ One-third of the Qur’an.” Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10058","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Qays, he said: I heard Amr bin Maimun talk, on the authority of Abu Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Does any of you often read a third of the Qur’an every night?” They said: Who can bear that? He said: “Say: He is God, One.” On the authority of Yusuf bin Saeed, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: Is any of you incapable? . . . . So he mentioned its meaning as suspended (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10059","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman bin Mawhib, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, that Abu Ayyub used to say: “Indeed, Allah is the One, the Eternal, the One-third of the Qur’an.”"
"10060","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Umayyah bin Khalid told me, he said: My nephew Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Umm Kulthum bint Uqba said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Say, ‘He is God, One.’” It is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an."
"10061","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: my uncle told us, he said: my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: he told me Al-Harith bin Fudayl Al-Ansari, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Zuhri, who said: Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf informed me that a group of The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him that they heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Say, ‘He is God, One,’” to be equal to a third. The Qur’an is for whoever prays by it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10062","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Sa’sa’ah, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that a man heard a man reciting: Say, He is God, One, repeating it. So when morning came, he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And it was mentioned to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an.” Ismail bin Jafar disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10063","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahdam told us, he said: Ismail bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas And he mentioned a word that means it, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Sa’sa’a. And Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ismail bin Jafar told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Sa’sa’ah al-Mazni, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, he said: Qatada bin al-Nu’man told me, In the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man used to recite from magic: “Say, ‘He is God.’” He repeated it and did not add anything more. When morning came, a man came. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, so-and-so got up during the night and recited from dawn: Say, He is God, One. {1} God, the Eternal, the Eternal. { 2 } He did not beget, nor was He ever begotten { 3 } And there was no one equal to Him { 4 } He repeats it, not adding to it, as if he were just saying it? The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an.” The wording of the hadith is from Zakaria (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"10064","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, that he told them on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ma'dan, on the authority of Abu al-Darda', on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Is not one of you able to read a third of the Qur’an in one night?” They said: We are weaker and more incapable than that. He said: “Indeed, God divided the Qur’an into three parts, so He made Say: He is God, One, one of the parts.” The Qur’an"
"10065","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ubaid, a client of the family of Zayd bin Al-Khattab, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: We arrived with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard a man reciting: Say, He is God, One. {1} God Al-Samad {2} He did not beget nor was he ever begotten {3} And there was no one equal to Him {4} Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is obligatory,” so I asked him: What, O Messenger of God? He said: “Paradise.”"
